# Security policy — {{CANONICAL_NAME}}

This framework child inherits CrownThrive security, privacy, IP, rights and repository-federation controls from `{{PARENT_REPOSITORY}}`.

## Non-negotiables

- No production secrets, service-role keys, provider tokens, private keys or recovery phrases in Git.
- No proprietary calibration, private evaluation corpora or restricted evidence bodies in public/customer-facing artifacts.
- GitHub Actions OIDC is the repository-federation authentication mechanism.
- The child cannot self-certify or expand its own authority.
- Agent D is the parent certification gate.
- D3 remains human-reserved.
- Security failures remain visible; do not disable checks to clear CI.

## Reporting and remediation

Record security findings through the governed CrownThrive issue/agent process. Preserve evidence privately where necessary. Public issue text must remain sanitized.

A private repository is not by itself evidence that content is appropriately classified. Apply the parent IP/disclosure and security rules to every artifact.
